WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.870
x squared plus y squared minus
six x plus four y equals twelve.

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.150
It doesn't look like anything familiar.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.800
So test points one by one, and
plot every point that fits.

4
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.340
Dot after dot, a shape appears.

5
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.480
It's a circle.

6
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.600
So where is its centre, when the
equation never seems to mention it?

7
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.680
In this mission, you'll build the
equation of a circle from Pythagoras.

8
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.150
You'll read the centre
straight from that equation,

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.690
with the signs reversed.

10
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.570
And you'll complete the square,
in x and in y separately,

11
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.440
to turn an expanded equation
back into that readable form.

12
00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: find the centre of
the circle hiding in this equation.
